WEBVTT


00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.513
You're dead! You're fucking dead!


00:02:26.599 --> 00:02:28.078
I'll get my brother!


00:02:28.159 --> 00:02:32.471
- Jen, come back! Wait!
- Fucking pervert!


00:02:32.559 --> 00:02:36.552
If that was a joke,
it wasn't very fucking funny.


00:02:36.639 --> 00:02:39.437
I'd look out for her brother.
He's a fucking mentalist.


00:02:39.519 --> 00:02:42.430
Jen! Jen!


00:03:59.793 --> 00:04:02.943
- I'll miss you.
- I hate you.


00:04:03.032 --> 00:04:06.503
Can I take this?
This can't still fit you, surely?


00:04:06.593 --> 00:04:09.345
- Get out of my room, Hallam.
- Not without these.


00:04:09.432 --> 00:04:11.150
- Hallam!
- I'm gonna take these,


00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:13.792
- and what if I put these back? Ow!
- Get out of my room.


00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:30.255
Thank you.


00:05:31.266 --> 00:05:35.145
To Australia and great adventures.


00:05:35.227 --> 00:05:37.296
And happy anniversary, Dad and Verity.


00:05:38.186 --> 00:05:40.222
Absent friends.


00:05:41.545 --> 00:05:42.534
Absent friends.


00:05:49.305 --> 00:05:51.660
Do you know why
we chose this restaurant?


00:05:51.745 --> 00:05:55.021
- It can't be the food.
- I told you to have the veal.


00:05:55.105 --> 00:06:00.098
It was here that Julius first
asked me to help manage the firm.


00:06:00.184 --> 00:06:03.335
You mean when you were the secretary?


00:06:03.424 --> 00:06:05.892
That's right, when I was his secretary.


00:06:05.984 --> 00:06:08.976
- I didn't know that.
- That's because I said no.


00:06:09.064 --> 00:06:10.383
I wasn't ready for it then.


00:06:10.464 --> 00:06:13.023
This afternoon,
I put the same question to Verity,


00:06:13.103 --> 00:06:15.901
- and I'm happy to say she agreed.
- Congratulations.


00:06:20.343 --> 00:06:22.299
When was it you were first asked?


00:06:24.062 --> 00:06:26.019
It must have been
a couple of years ago.


00:06:26.103 --> 00:06:28.741
And was that before or after?


00:06:31.782 --> 00:06:34.171
It wasn't long
before your mother passed away.


00:06:44.381 --> 00:06:47.737
Do you remember what happened later?
Your friend.


00:06:47.821 --> 00:06:51.655
Oh, yes.


00:06:51.741 --> 00:06:54.174
That same day,
an old boyfriend of mine calls up


00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:58.253
and insists on taking me out
for dinner. Guess where he took me.


00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:02.252
Can you imagine
what the staff must have thought?


00:07:02.339 --> 00:07:05.776
They probably
thought you were a prostitute.


00:07:13.859 --> 00:07:15.292
Probably.


00:07:20.738 --> 00:07:24.618
- Come to the pub.
- No, thanks. Here's fine.


00:07:24.699 --> 00:07:27.496
You got your binoculars in there?


00:07:27.578 --> 00:07:30.808
- Come to the pub.
- Maybe next time.


00:07:30.898 --> 00:07:33.855
There isn't gonna be a next time.


00:07:38.617 --> 00:07:40.812
You fucking splitter.


00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:18.168
Night, Mum.


00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:30.605
Hallam!


00:09:31.729 --> 00:09:33.640
I'm going!


00:09:35.928 --> 00:09:37.999
Bye!


00:09:48.527 --> 00:09:49.881
Lucy!


00:09:52.408 --> 00:09:55.683
Wait! Lucy!


00:10:25.366 --> 00:10:27.959
Hallam, lunch is ready.


00:10:36.365 --> 00:10:38.242
It's very good soup.


00:10:40.924 --> 00:10:43.154
We've been thinking,
now that Lucy's gone,


00:10:43.244 --> 00:10:47.795
it's not good for you to be here
with no one of your own age around.


00:10:49.324 --> 00:10:52.713
Too much time to dwell on things.


00:10:52.803 --> 00:10:56.000
I have some contacts
in the wine trade in London, and...


00:10:56.083 --> 00:10:59.359
You'll have a chance to make
new friends, earn a bit of money,


00:10:59.443 --> 00:11:02.037
learn something you'll enjoy
the rest of your life,


00:11:02.123 --> 00:11:04.842
and it'll be a good
stop-gap before college.


00:11:04.923 --> 00:11:07.800
Actually, I've decided
not to go to college.


00:11:07.882 --> 00:11:12.034
- So what are you going to do?
- I'm staying right here.


00:11:12.962 --> 00:11:15.920
So I'm sorry if that
screws up your plans.


00:12:25.757 --> 00:12:27.986
It's as if this place is still hers.


00:12:28.076 --> 00:12:31.751
We agreed you could make
whatever changes you want, and you are.


00:12:31.836 --> 00:12:34.669
- You know what I want most?
- What?


00:12:39.595 --> 00:12:41.552
- Look, he doesn't hate you.
- He does.


00:12:41.636 --> 00:12:45.150
He doesn't. You just have to be patient.


00:12:49.035 --> 00:12:51.310
I think that
I should go away for a while.


00:12:55.314 --> 00:12:58.465
I'll deal with Hallam. All right?


00:13:19.753 --> 00:13:24.143
- Where's Verity?
- She's gone to see a friend.


00:13:26.352 --> 00:13:28.024
Are you in the dog house?


00:13:30.112 --> 00:13:31.942
What is it, Hallam?


00:13:32.031 --> 00:13:34.704
- I found Mum's old boat in the loch.
- Did you?


00:13:34.791 --> 00:13:39.387
- Good God! I thought it was sunk.
- It had.


00:13:39.471 --> 00:13:43.258
When she took me out in it,
how long was that before she died?


00:13:43.351 --> 00:13:45.228
About a month. Why?


00:13:45.311 --> 00:13:47.347
Were you fucking Verity by then?


00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:52.462
That's what "Fancy a stroll"
was about. Christ, I'm a fool.


00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:55.587
- You haven't answered the question.
- Not even close, Hal.


00:13:55.670 --> 00:13:57.945
I was busy trying
to keep the show on the road.


00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:01.340
When you found her, had she tied
her hands and weighed herself down?


00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:03.863
- Where's this coming from?
- People who can swim,


00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:06.338
it's hard to drown. Instincts take over.


00:14:06.429 --> 00:14:11.549
- Who told you that?
- I did some research, all right?


00:14:13.829 --> 00:14:18.266
At the time, I decided to spare you
some of the details from the inquest.


00:14:21.588 --> 00:14:25.263
Before she came out here,


00:14:25.348 --> 00:14:29.056
your mother took
an overdose of sleeping pills.


00:14:32.947 --> 00:14:37.020
- Thanks for fucking telling me.
- I'm sorry.


00:14:38.147 --> 00:14:42.425
I know it's hard, but you
have got to try to pick up the pieces.


00:14:42.507 --> 00:14:45.067
Well, I can see it didn't
take you very long, did it?


00:14:45.147 --> 00:14:47.660
Hal, this won't help.


00:14:52.306 --> 00:14:54.296
So it definitely wasn't an accident?


00:14:55.785 --> 00:14:57.298
No.


00:14:58.705 --> 00:14:59.934
It wasn't.


00:15:34.583 --> 00:15:38.416
Oh, no! I've painted
over his mum's face.


00:15:38.502 --> 00:15:40.220
Paint all over it.


00:15:40.302 --> 00:15:43.180
- Give it here, I'll do it.
- It's a single ticket.


00:15:47.142 --> 00:15:49.098
Fuck off, man. Go!


00:17:04.577 --> 00:17:06.726
<i>- Hallam?
- Lucy?</i>


00:17:09.776 --> 00:17:12.414
<i>- Are you still there? Hello?
- Can you hear me?</i>


00:17:16.416 --> 00:17:21.091
What if someone else gave her the pills?
Spiked her drink or something?


00:17:21.775 --> 00:17:24.687
Well, don't you think
she's capable of it?


00:17:24.775 --> 00:17:26.731
Why is that paranoid?


00:17:28.615 --> 00:17:31.687
Of course I miss you.
Oh, she'd love that.


00:17:31.775 --> 00:17:34.926
She's already twisting Dad's arm
to try and get rid of me.


00:18:44.009 --> 00:18:45.761
Hello!


00:18:48.569 --> 00:18:50.685
I see you've had some visitors.


00:18:51.369 --> 00:18:53.484
- Can I come up?
- No way.


00:19:15.607 --> 00:19:17.483
You left these on your bed.


00:19:20.927 --> 00:19:25.522
"Today, walking past the office,
I saw Dad stroking Verity's back.


00:19:25.607 --> 00:19:27.642
It made me ponder his evening strolls".


00:19:27.726 --> 00:19:29.478
- Not allowed.
- "I followed.


00:19:29.566 --> 00:19:33.353
There she was, bouncing up and down.
I couldn't take my eyes off the dimple


00:19:33.445 --> 00:19:38.200
that appeared on her shoulder
every time she clawed at his neck.


00:19:38.286 --> 00:19:43.882
I hate myself, but I want to
bury my face in that little cushion".


00:19:43.965 --> 00:19:46.080
Give me my diaries back.


00:19:46.165 --> 00:19:48.599
Hallam, you really need to move on.


00:19:48.684 --> 00:19:51.324
I know Julius will feel the same
when he reads these.


00:19:51.405 --> 00:19:53.042
No, they're private diaries!


00:19:53.124 --> 00:19:56.400
So are bedrooms. By volume two,
you peeped in half the village's.


00:19:56.484 --> 00:19:59.681
I wonder what the local paper
would do with that,


00:19:59.764 --> 00:20:02.756
- or the police for that matter.
- The police?


00:20:02.843 --> 00:20:05.563
Wonder what they'll think
when I tell them about you.


00:20:05.644 --> 00:20:07.281
Me?


00:20:08.524 --> 00:20:10.673
Recognise this?


00:20:10.763 --> 00:20:11.991
It's a hammer, Hallam.


00:20:12.083 --> 00:20:16.315
The same hammer that sunk my mother's
boat once you'd drugged her coffee.


00:20:24.402 --> 00:20:26.996
She wanted to die, Hallam.


00:20:27.081 --> 00:20:29.596
You tell me what you did to her!


00:21:58.715 --> 00:22:01.752
It's time to fly the nest, Hallam,


00:22:01.835 --> 00:22:03.790
and I think you know that.


00:22:54.311 --> 00:22:56.541
Spare some change, please.


00:24:25.305 --> 00:24:29.058
- It's a fucking shite hole.
- I didn't want to come here.


00:24:29.144 --> 00:24:32.420
Stick your fucking castle
right up your fucking arse.


00:24:32.504 --> 00:24:34.813
What do you want?


00:24:34.904 --> 00:24:37.099
Thirty, 35?


00:24:37.944 --> 00:24:39.297
Thirty-five?


00:24:41.583 --> 00:24:44.144
Well, go on, fuck off, then!


00:24:44.224 --> 00:24:45.372
Fuck off, then!


00:24:46.623 --> 00:24:48.454
Whoa.


00:24:48.543 --> 00:24:51.296
- What's your name, son?
- Carl.


00:24:51.383 --> 00:24:55.011
- Where's home, Carl?
- I'm staying with a friend.


00:24:55.102 --> 00:24:57.139
Not that gentleman
you were talking to?


00:24:57.222 --> 00:25:01.215
- No.
- So, your friend, what's his address?


00:25:28.140 --> 00:25:30.779
Where the hell is he?


00:26:29.616 --> 00:26:31.173
Mum!


00:27:49.010 --> 00:27:50.568
Can I help you?


00:27:55.649 --> 00:27:57.879
Do you have any jobs, please?


00:27:57.969 --> 00:28:00.961
Sorry, we use an agency.
I can give you their details.


00:28:01.049 --> 00:28:02.528
Thanks.


00:28:10.728 --> 00:28:12.719
Why are you staring at me?


00:28:12.808 --> 00:28:16.847
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to. I've never
been for a job interview before,


00:28:16.928 --> 00:28:20.966
and I was just wondering if you could
give me some advice on how to do it.


00:28:21.047 --> 00:28:24.802
- I'm sorry?
- Would you...?


00:28:24.887 --> 00:28:28.038
Could you throw a couple
of practise questions at me, just...


00:28:28.127 --> 00:28:29.719
...just for practise?


00:28:32.847 --> 00:28:36.999
- How desperate are you for work?
- Pretty desperate.


00:28:37.087 --> 00:28:40.965
Well, the highest turnover in jobs
is usually in kitchen porters.


00:28:41.046 --> 00:28:44.516
- OK. I'll be a kitchen porter.
- Why do you think you'd be suitable?


00:28:44.606 --> 00:28:47.518
Well, it's what I've wanted to do
ever since I was a kid.


00:28:47.605 --> 00:28:49.323
Sit down.


00:28:51.885 --> 00:28:55.002
Don't tell people
what you think they want to hear.


00:28:55.085 --> 00:28:57.804
- Just be yourself.
- OK.


00:28:57.885 --> 00:29:00.922
I'm very enthusiastic
and I'm a quick learner,


00:29:01.005 --> 00:29:03.155
and I'll work days, nights, weekends,


00:29:03.244 --> 00:29:05.314
any overtime you want
for no extra money.


00:29:05.404 --> 00:29:09.716
It would be illegal for you
to work overtime for no extra money.


00:29:09.804 --> 00:29:12.193
Well, give me a week's trial,
a day's trial.


00:29:12.284 --> 00:29:14.434
I want a chance
to get a foot on the ladder.


00:29:14.524 --> 00:29:17.322
If everything works out,
you won't pay agency fees.


00:29:17.404 --> 00:29:20.315
That's a win-win situation for you.


00:29:26.363 --> 00:29:30.355
Remember what I said about
the fast turnover in kitchen porters?


00:29:31.403 --> 00:29:34.236
You're about to meet the exception.


00:29:35.282 --> 00:29:38.911
- Cutlery, handles up.
- Right.


00:29:39.002 --> 00:29:40.275
Go on.


00:29:43.281 --> 00:29:47.832
Hey, hey, hey! What is the hurry?
Trying to show me up on your first day?


00:29:47.921 --> 00:29:49.559
No.


00:29:49.641 --> 00:29:53.873
I fucking hate this job,
but it's my job.


00:29:53.961 --> 00:29:55.440
Do you understand?


00:29:57.041 --> 00:29:58.871
I killed a man once.


00:29:58.960 --> 00:30:01.350
Smashed his skull on a pier.


00:30:02.480 --> 00:30:03.993
Just so you know.


00:30:23.679 --> 00:30:26.238
You take the rest. I'm off for a smoke.


00:32:46.429 --> 00:32:49.898
Don't make friends with the chefs,
otherwise they'll want favours.


00:32:49.988 --> 00:32:51.819
But don't get on their bad side,


00:32:51.908 --> 00:32:55.696
or you'll be cleaning out
the fat fryer on a quiet Thursday.


00:32:56.428 --> 00:33:00.467
They're all cunts anyway.
Except TJ. He's OK.


00:33:00.548 --> 00:33:02.458
Even if he is a fucking bullshitter.


00:33:02.547 --> 00:33:06.586
Have you ever met an African over here
who wasn't a brain surgeon over there?


00:33:06.667 --> 00:33:09.385
Are you listening to me?


00:33:11.307 --> 00:33:13.740
Yes, of course.


00:33:13.826 --> 00:33:16.943
Brain surgeon. African. Cunt.


00:33:17.026 --> 00:33:19.938
Aye, cunt.


00:33:35.665 --> 00:33:39.134
Reach out. One, two.
One. Right knee.


00:38:42.242 --> 00:38:44.837
- Hey! Ho!
- Raymond!


00:38:44.922 --> 00:38:46.514
- Hey!
- Hey!


00:38:46.602 --> 00:38:50.561
Oh-ho! That's gonna cost you.


00:38:50.642 --> 00:38:52.758
- Really?
- Yeah.


00:38:56.481 --> 00:39:00.270
- Are you serious?
- Absolutely.


00:39:08.001 --> 00:39:09.559
Come on. You're losing.


00:39:15.641 --> 00:39:17.039
That's ¡Ì4.


00:39:21.120 --> 00:39:24.157
- Do you mind if I take a break?
- Do what the fuck you like.

